        "description": "<p>It will embed your google map into a widget area. You can add a widget in any of your widget areas and It will show your map.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<h4>From the dashboard:</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to the WordPress Dashboard &#8220;Add New Plugin&#8221; section</li>\n<li>Search For &#8220;Widget for Google Map&#8221;</li>\n<li>Install, then Activate it</li>\n</ol>\n<h4>From the control panel:</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>Unzip (if it is zipped) and Upload <code>widget-for-google-map</code> folder to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code> directory</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; menu in WordPress</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='is%20there%20need%20anything%20to%20do%20with%20my%20theme%3F'>\nIs there need anything to do with my theme?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>No, you can not do anything, It will be work automatically with your widget area.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='does%20it%20work%20with%20any%20theme%3F'>\nDoes it work with any theme?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Absolutely! It will work with any theme where WordPress works.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial stable realese</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
